  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"0.8.1\"\n\npackage:\n  name: rig\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/r-lib/rig/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: a0f00e7c84573c15819cf7d907dd8668ad67a31784b07e1edd59039e514675fd\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n  script:\n    env:\n      CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_LTO: fat\n      CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_STRIP: symbols\n    content:\n      - if: unix\n        then:\n          - cargo auditable install --path=. --root=\"$PREFIX\" --no-track --locked --bins --target-dir=target\n          # copy shell completion files\n          - mkdir -p \"$PREFIX\"/share/bash-completion/completions \"$PREFIX\"/share/fish/vendor_completions.d \"$PREFIX\"/share/zsh/site-functions\n          - find target -name rig.bash -exec cp \\{\\} \"$PREFIX\"/share/bash-completion/completions/rig \\;\n          - find target -name rig.fish -exec cp \\{\\} \"$PREFIX\"/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/rig.fish \\;\n          - find target -name _rig     -exec cp \\{\\} \"$PREFIX\"/share/zsh/site-functions/_rig \\;\n      - if: win\n        then:\n          - cargo auditable install --path=. --root=\"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\" --no-track --locked --bins --target-dir=target\n          # copy shell completion files\n          - mkdir \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\"\\share\\bash-completion\\completions\n          - mkdir \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\"\\share\\fish\\vendor_completions.d\n          - mkdir \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\"\\share\\zsh\\site-functions\n          - for /f \"usebackq\" %%f in (`dir /s /b target\\rig.bash`) do (copy \"%%f\" \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\\share\\bash-completion\\completions\\rig\")\n          - for /f \"usebackq\" %%f in (`dir /s /b target\\rig.fish`) do (copy \"%%f\" \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\\share\\fish\\vendor_completions.d\\rig.fish\")\n          - for /f \"usebackq\" %%f in (`dir /s /b target\\_rig`)     do (copy \"%%f\" \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\\share\\zsh\\site-functions\\_rig\")\n      - cargo-bundle-licenses --format=yaml --output=./THIRDPARTY.yml\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('rust') }}\n    - cargo-auditable\n    - cargo-bundle-licenses\n\ntests:\n  - script:\n      - rig --help\n      - rig --version\n  - package_contents:\n      bin:\n        - rig\n      files:\n        - if: unix\n          then:\n            - share/bash-completion/completions/rig\n            - share/fish/vendor_completions.d/rig.fish\n            - share/zsh/site-functions/_rig\n        - if: win\n          then:\n            - Library/share/bash-completion/completions/rig\n            - Library/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/rig.fish\n            - Library/share/zsh/site-functions/_rig\n      strict: true\n\nabout:\n  summary: The R Installation Manager\n  description: |\n    rig is a CLI to install, remove, configure, and switch between multiple\n    versions of R. It works on macOS, Windows and Linux, supports symbolic\n    version names (e.g. `release`, `devel`, `oldrel`), lets you run multiple\n    R versions in parallel via quick links, and integrates with the\n    RStudio and Positron IDEs.\n  license: MIT\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - THIRDPARTY.yml\n  homepage: https://r-lib.github.io/rig/\n  repository: https://github.com/r-lib/rig\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - salim-b\n",
